00:37:57,129 --> 00:37:59,871
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, if you were to clarify it enough, then you stop doing even that.

441
00:38:00,411 --> 00:38:14,800
[SPEAKER_00]: And that was in one of the letters, early, early letters, and, you know, he mentioned that, and he was talking about consciousness, and he was, he was often quoting Sartre, and so on, and then he, in one of the letters, he kind of realized, oh, actually, no, I think, I think,

442
00:38:16,323 --> 00:38:18,345
[SPEAKER_00]: I think I've been fully, kind of, just...

443
00:38:18,425 --> 00:38:30,193
[SPEAKER_00]: I picked it up from Sartre or something, but I was assuming that Consciousness is always me, as opposed to... or here, as opposed to over there, but Consciousness is on the level of the five aggregates, so to speak.

444
00:38:30,274 --> 00:38:41,382
[SPEAKER_00]: So, basically, then he realized that, oh, well, if I'm correcting what I just wrote, that means I might have kind of abandoned the view of my Consciousness being myself.

445
00:38:42,238 --> 00:38:44,339
[SPEAKER_00]: And if that's true, that's very welcome.

446
00:38:44,419 --> 00:38:47,840
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, the next life, you follow another insight, and another insight, and another insight.

447
00:38:47,860 --> 00:38:49,561
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's how you build it up.

448
00:38:51,362 --> 00:38:53,562
[SPEAKER_01]: Like you just started making sense to him, basically.

449
00:38:53,582 --> 00:38:57,564
[SPEAKER_01]: It wasn't like something he took on faith and repeated, repeated, repeated.

450
00:38:57,884 --> 00:38:58,544
[SPEAKER_00]: No, no, no.

451
00:38:58,564 --> 00:38:59,285
[SPEAKER_00]: Because, eh...

452
00:39:00,025 --> 00:39:02,526
[SPEAKER_00]: I guess some people could perhaps just take something on faith.

453
00:39:03,246 --> 00:39:08,268
[SPEAKER_00]: But, whether you take it on faith, or whether you can approach it with sort of critical reflection, and so on,

454
00:39:09,266 --> 00:39:11,646
[SPEAKER_00]: You have to arrive at the same point, which is to understand it.

455
00:39:12,027 --> 00:39:17,447
[SPEAKER_00]: So, often people are too lazy, mentally, to make the effort to understand things.

456
00:39:17,467 --> 00:39:19,668
[SPEAKER_00]: They say, oh, I'm not that type.

457
00:39:20,148 --> 00:39:22,608
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm kind of the faith type, or sādhā.

458
00:39:22,988 --> 00:39:24,069
[SPEAKER_00]: I follow sādhā and stuff.

459
00:39:24,329 --> 00:39:25,369
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, so what do you do then?

460
00:39:25,549 --> 00:39:27,509
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you still making effort to understand through your faith?

461
00:39:28,609 --> 00:39:29,950
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you realize most of them don't.

